  "note": "The name Isaac is explained by laughter using צחק in Genesis 21:6. Its occasional spelling יִשְׂחָק overlaps the verb here, but the name belongs with צחק. Akkadian ṣiāhu, Oracc armep/x000025400, likewise means laugh, though the sound correspondence with this spelling is uncertain. The Syriac root with shin means harass or wear down."
